  "title": "Kojiki",
  "summary": "The Kojiki (Records of Ancient Matters) is a three-book account of Japanese myth and early court history. Ō no Yasumaro compiled it in 712 and presented it to Empress Genmei, after Emperor Tenmu had started the project. It is counted among the earliest written Japanese chronicles.",
